  "rendered_prompt": "<|system|>You are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|end|><|user|>Paragraph:\n\"\"\"\nIn The Outsiders, Ponyboy learns that people are more alike than they seem. At the start of the novel, he believes that the Socs, the rich kids from the west side, have perfect lives with no problems. Then he meets Cherry Valance, a Soc girl who tells him that rich kids have troubles too. Later, Randy, another Soc, admits that he is tired of all the fighting between the two groups. These conversations make Ponyboy realize that the line between Greasers and Socs is not as clear as he thought. S. E. Hinton shows that judging people by their group keeps us from seeing who they really are.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer wants to use the word \"stereotype\" in this essay.\n\nWrite 5 different sentences that use \"stereotype\" naturally and could fit into this paragraph, on its topic and in its argument. Each sentence must contain \"stereotype\" (another form of the word, such as a plural or past tense, is fine). Use only ideas the paragraph already contains; do not invent statistics, names or quotations. Put the best sentences first.<|end|><|assistant|>",
